
# Chihuahua
key[]: "chih_pregui_desc"
val[]: "The Pegüis Canyon is a dramatic gorge carved by the Conchos River near Ojinaga, Chihuahua. Its limestone walls rise above a winding river corridor in the Chihuahuan Desert."

key[]: "chih_chih_desc"
val[]: "Chihuahua is the capital and largest city of the state of the same name. Its historic center, industry and position on northern Mexico's main routes make it a regional hub."

key[]: "chih_tutu_desc"
val[]: "Tutuaca is a protected natural area in western Chihuahua. Its mountains, pine-oak forests and deep ravines shelter wildlife typical of the Sierra Madre Occidental."

key[]: "chih_pinos_desc"
val[]: "Pinos Altos is a historic mining district in the mountains of western Chihuahua. Gold and silver extraction shaped the area's settlements and roads."

key[]: "chih_mirab_desc"
val[]: "This viewpoint overlooks the wooded Barranca de Candameña and the area around Basaseachi Falls, one of the best-known landscapes in the Sierra Madre Occidental."

key[]: "chih_tara_desc"
val[]: "The Sierra Tarahumara forms part of the Sierra Madre Occidental in Chihuahua. It is known for vast forests, high plateaus and the canyon country inhabited by the Rarámuri people."

key[]: "chih_creel_desc"
val[]: "Creel is a mountain town and an important gateway to the Copper Canyon region. Rail travel, Rarámuri culture and nearby rock formations make it a popular base for visitors."

key[]: "chih_sierra_desc"
val[]: "The Sierra Madre Occidental is an extensive mountain system running through western Mexico. Forested plateaus are cut by deep canyons and volcanic valleys."

key[]: "chih_divi_desc"
val[]: "The Copper Canyon is a network of large canyons in the Sierra Tarahumara. Viewpoints near Divisadero reveal immense cliffs, forests and valleys crossed by the Chihuahua al Pacífico railway."

key[]: "chih_uriquem_desc"
val[]: "This viewpoint looks into the Urique Canyon, one of the deepest ravines in the Copper Canyon system, with steep slopes descending toward the Urique River."

key[]: "chih_urique_desc"
val[]: "Urique lies at the bottom of a deep canyon beside the river of the same name. Its warm climate contrasts with the cool pine-covered highlands above."

key[]: "chih_bato_desc"
val[]: "Batopilas is a historic mining town set deep in the Sierra Tarahumara. Its narrow streets, old buildings and riverside setting preserve the character of an isolated canyon settlement."

key[]: "chih_batob_desc"
val[]: "Batopilas Canyon descends from the high forests of Chihuahua to a warm subtropical valley. The winding road reveals steep slopes, cliffs and remote communities."

key[]: "chih_uriqueb_desc"
val[]: "Urique Canyon is one of the great ravines of the Sierra Tarahumara. The Urique River flows far below high plateaus connected by demanding mountain roads."

key[]: "chih_verde_desc"
val[]: "The Río Verde crosses rugged country in western Mexico, forming a green river corridor among dry slopes and mountain valleys."

key[]: "chih_deli_desc"
val[]: "Delicias is an agricultural and industrial city in central Chihuahua. Irrigation transformed the surrounding valley into one of the state's main farming areas."


# Durango
key[]: "dgo_piax_desc"
val[]: "The Piaxtla Canyon follows the rugged drainage of the Piaxtla River in the Sierra Madre Occidental, where mountain roads cross forests, ravines and remote settlements."

key[]: "dgo_sant_desc"
val[]: "Santiago Papasquiaro occupies a broad valley surrounded by the mountains of Durango. Agriculture, forestry and regional trade have long shaped the town and its landscape."


# Sinaloa
key[]: "sin_comedero_desc"
val[]: "The José López Portillo Dam, widely known as El Comedero, holds back the San Lorenzo River in Sinaloa. Its reservoir winds between steep, green mountain slopes."


# Durango
key[]: "dgo_espinazo_desc"
val[]: "The Espinazo del Diablo is a celebrated mountain section of the Durango-Mazatlán road. Tight curves, deep ravines and changing weather define this crossing of the Sierra Madre Occidental."

key[]: "dgo_baluarte_desc"
val[]: "The Baluarte Bicentennial Bridge carries the Durango-Mazatlán highway across a deep ravine on the Durango-Sinaloa border. Its tall cable-stayed span is a landmark of the mountain route."


# Nayarit
key[]: "nay_nayar_desc"
val[]: "The Sierra del Nayar is a rugged region of canyons, rivers and wooded highlands in Nayarit. It is also an important cultural homeland of the Náayeri people."

key[]: "nay_blas_desc"
val[]: "San Blas is a historic Pacific port in Nayarit. Its pier faces an area known for beaches, mangroves, wetlands and abundant birdlife."


# Durango
key[]: "dgo_pena_desc"
val[]: "Peña del Águila is a prominent mountain landmark whose rocky summit rises over the surrounding highland landscape."


# Zacatecas
key[]: "zac_morones_desc"
val[]: "The Sierra de Morones forms a rugged mountainous landscape in southern Zacatecas, with rocky ridges, ravines and seasonal streams."


# Chihuahua
key[]: "chih_basa_desc"
val[]: "Basaseachi Falls drops from the Duraznos and Basaseachi streams into the Barranca de Candameña. The 246-meter waterfall is one of Mexico's highest and the centerpiece of a national park."


# Sonora
key[]: "son_cananeam_desc"
val[]: "The Cananea mining district in northern Sonora is closely linked to large-scale copper production. Terraced open pits and processing facilities dominate the industrial landscape."

key[]: "son_caridad_desc"
val[]: "La Caridad is a large open-pit copper mine near Nacozari de García, Sonora. Its benches, haul roads and processing complex form a vast engineered landscape."

key[]: "son_gmexico_desc"
val[]: "This industrial complex processes minerals from Sonora's copper-mining region. Large plants, conveyors and storage areas reflect the scale of production around Nacozari."

key[]: "son_nacozari_desc"
val[]: "Nacozari de García is a mining town in northeastern Sonora. It was renamed in honor of railway engineer Jesús García, remembered for preventing a greater disaster in 1907."

key[]: "son_juriquipa_desc"
val[]: "The Sierra de Juriquipa is part of the rugged mountain country of northeastern Sonora, where desert foothills rise toward oak and grassland habitats."

key[]: "son_mmaria_desc"
val[]: "The María Mine is part of northern Sonora's long-established copper-mining region, marked by open workings, service roads and mineral-processing infrastructure."

key[]: "son_pinito_desc"
val[]: "Sierra El Pinito is one of the isolated mountain ranges that break the desert plains of northern Sonora, creating cooler highland habitats above the valleys."

key[]: "son_cieneguita_desc"
val[]: "Sierra La Cieneguita rises from the dry landscapes of northern Mexico, adding rocky ridges and elevated grasslands to the surrounding desert scenery."

key[]: "son_pajarito_desc"
val[]: "Sierra El Pajarito is a rugged range in northern Sonora, where rocky slopes and upland vegetation overlook broad desert valleys."

key[]: "son_yaqui_desc"
val[]: "The Yaqui River drains much of eastern Sonora. Near Sierra Los Chinos, its valley cuts through rugged terrain before continuing toward the agricultural plains and the Gulf of California."


# Arizona
key[]: "az_lavender_desc"
val[]: "The Lavender Pit is a large open-pit copper mine in Bisbee, Arizona. Its stepped benches expose bands of colorful rock beside the historic mining town."


# Chihuahua
key[]: "chih_majalca_desc"
val[]: "Cumbres de Majalca is a protected mountain area north of Chihuahua City, known for unusual rock formations, pine-oak woodland and cool highland scenery."

key[]: "chih_puertosl_desc"
val[]: "This mountain pass crosses the Sierra de San Luis, a remote range of grasslands, oak woodland and rocky peaks near the Chihuahua-Sonora border."


# Sinaloa
key[]: "sin_culiacanl_desc"
val[]: "This distribution center represents Culiacán's role as a logistics hub for the productive valleys of central Sinaloa."

key[]: "sin_culiacan2_desc"
val[]: "Culiacán Rosales is the capital of Sinaloa. The city stands where the Humaya and Tamazula rivers meet to form the Culiacán River."


# Durango
key[]: "dgo_temohaya1_desc"
val[]: "Temohaya Canyon cuts through the rugged highlands of Durango, revealing steep wooded slopes and the complex relief of the Sierra Madre Occidental."

key[]: "dgo_temohaya2_desc"
val[]: "This panorama opens across the Temohaya highlands, where forested ridges and deep valleys stretch through the mountains of Durango."

key[]: "dgo_temohaya3_desc"
val[]: "The Temohaya crest follows high terrain in the Sierra Madre Occidental and offers broad views over successive ridges and ravines."

key[]: "dgo_quebradas1_desc"
val[]: "Las Quebradas is the name given to the deep canyon country of western Durango. From the highlands, the land falls sharply toward the Pacific lowlands."

key[]: "dgo_quebradas2_desc"
val[]: "The river at Las Quebradas winds through a remote canyon landscape, linking the forested heights of Durango with warmer valleys downstream."

key[]: "dgo_mezquital1_desc"
val[]: "The Mezquital Valley lies among the mountains and canyons of southern Durango. The river corridor supports settlements and vegetation within an otherwise rugged region."

key[]: "dgo_tepe1_desc"
val[]: "Tepetatita Canyon is one of the steep ravines carved into the Sierra Madre Occidental, with winding roads, rocky walls and forested slopes."


